Ladybird caps each serialized history state at 16 MiB, and drops the
states of a session history’s oldest entries once its states add up
past 512 MiB. Run in Chrome 157, Firefox 151, and WebKit 26.5: Firefox
throws past 16 MiB for a single state (nsDocShell::AddState(), the
browser.history.maxStateObjectSize pref), and Chrome and WebKit don’t.
WebKit instead throws a QuotaExceededError once a document’s states
pass 64 MB in all (History::updateAndCheckStateObjectQuota()). Chrome
and Firefox bound the total by keeping at most 50 entries (Blink’s
kMaxSessionHistoryEntries, Gecko’s browser.sessionhistory.max_entries
pref), dropping the oldest whole. None of them nulls a state while
keeping its entry, so that part is Ladybird’s own.
